From aa81742f2bb1ee988353a64de91404f727b31ecc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:25:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tls: Pipeline TLS 1.2 splice receive and cover async I/O
 paths

TLS 1.2 recvmsg already submits independent decryptions concurrently,
but splice and read_sock wait for each record. Extend the buffered RX
pipeline to those readers so an asynchronous cipher can decrypt up to
eight available records before waiting, just as for TLS 1.3.

Keep TLS 1.2 recvmsg's direct-to-user async path. A recvmsg following a
buffered reader first drains rx_pending before resuming that path, so
partial splice, peek and receive can safely alternate. Ordered batch
processing preserves authenticated prefixes and defers later failures.

Add existing-harness tests for bulk send, MSG_MORE, bulk transmit splice,
SPLICE_F_MORE, receive splice/peek/recv transitions, and corrupted records
in receive splice. Run these across TLS cipher/version variants. Document
RX and TX pipeline behavior and the completion requirements of send calls.

Validation in QEMU TCG with pcrypt, KASAN and lockdep:
- All 117 focused tests passed, including new I/O and rekey coverage.
- Function traces show overlapping requests for send, transmit splice,
  recv and receive splice with both TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3. MORE variants
  also overlap; every traced request completed and no trace was lost.
- Each RX benchmark trial submitted/completed 128 decryptions. TLS 1.2
  splice reached eight in flight, excluding its untimed recv preflight.
- Kernel/selftest builds, diff checks and checkpatch passed.

OpenAI Codex assisted with implementation, validation and this changelog
in response to a request for pipelining in both directions, covering
splice/recv/send and TLS 1.2/1.3.

(cherry picked from commit fbc7d9a713fce51c16bb2dd1a450fcc26b7dcc60)
---
 include/net/tls.h |  2 +-
 net/tls/tls_sw.c  | 11 ++++++++---
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/net/tls.h b/include/net/tls.h
index 6833972f70a4..68ec4b06ecbb 100644
--- a/include/net/tls.h
+++ b/include/net/tls.h
@@ -131,7 +131,7 @@ struct tls_sw_context_rx {
 	struct crypto_aead *aead_recv;
 	struct crypto_wait async_wait;
 	struct sk_buff_head rx_list;	/* list of decrypted 'data' records */
-	struct list_head rx_pending;	/* TLS 1.3 records, in wire order */
+	struct list_head rx_pending;	/* buffered records, in wire order */
 	void (*saved_data_ready)(struct sock *sk);
 
 	u8 reader_present;
diff --git a/net/tls/tls_sw.c b/net/tls/tls_sw.c
index ffdc6486837a..8a7e29b690d0 100644
--- a/net/tls/tls_sw.c
+++ b/net/tls/tls_sw.c
@@ -2095,9 +2095,14 @@ static int tls_rx_one_record(struct sock *sk, struct msghdr *msg,
 	struct strp_msg *rxm;
 	int err;
 
-	/* Drain queued records if a BPF parser was attached after collection. */
-	if (ctx->async_capable && prot->version == TLS_1_3_VERSION &&
-	    tls_ctx->rx_conf == TLS_SW &&
+	/* Keep TLS 1.2 recvmsg's direct-to-user async path. Splice and
+	 * read_sock need authenticated kernel buffers, as does a recvmsg
+	 * which follows a reader that has already collected a batch.
+	 * If a BPF parser was attached, only drain already queued records.
+	 */
+	if (ctx->async_capable && tls_ctx->rx_conf == TLS_SW &&
+	    (prot->version == TLS_1_3_VERSION || !msg ||
+	     !list_empty(&ctx->rx_pending)) &&
 	    (!darg->no_async || !list_empty(&ctx->rx_pending))) {
 		err = tls_rx_decrypt_record(sk, darg);
 	} else {
